/* ============================================================================
   SILVER's ACES - the starter lines that ride on another family's party.

   Several starter regions share one of Silver's party families (see
   sRivalTrainerBase in src/starter_generation.c). Where they do, the family's
   own ace - its LAST mon - is replaced at battle time by the matching line
   below, chosen by sRivalAceBase. CYNDAQUIL's parties, for instance, serve
   Typhlosion as written and Blaziken, Infernape and Emboar from here.

   Each entry is a pseudo-trainer holding ONE mon, and only that mon is read
   (GetRivalAceOverride -> CreateNPCTrainerParty, src/battle_main.c). The
   header is there because trainerproc expects one; it is never shown. These
   constants are an enum of their own (include/constants/rival_aces.h), NOT
   trainer IDs, so this file costs no trainer IDs and no flags - the same
   arrangement as battle_partners.party.

   Rules, all checked by `py -3 .claude/rival_overlap.py`:
   - _1 .. _7 are the seven encounters, and a line's constants stay contiguous.
   - match the ace level of that encounter: 5 / 18 / 24 / 40 / 48 / 66 / 70.
   - carry what the other aces carry: nothing at 1-2 (the game fills the moves
     at battle time), four moves at 3-4, four moves and a held item at 5-7.
   - the ace must share no type with the family it rides on - at EVERY stage.
   - trainerproc does not check that a mon can learn its moves. The checker
     does, against canon, for every line written for Unova and Kalos.
   ============================================================================ */
